<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">United Arab States</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1958–1961</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The United Arab States was a loose confederation formed in March 1958 between the United Arab Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and the Mutawakkilite Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Imam Ahmad</a>. It had no real common institutions, and each member kept its own government. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Nasser</a> dissolved it in December 1961, after Syria's secession from the United Arab Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-arab-states.jpg" alt="United Arab States" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AlejandroFC · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:United_Arab_States_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
